# Template for infra/production/migrate.env, which is NOT in git. Read by
# the migrate service ALONE (docs/17 F52, 2026-10-02).
#
#   cp infra/production/migrate.env.example infra/production/migrate.env
#   chown root:root infra/production/migrate.env
#   chmod 600      infra/production/migrate.env
#
# `sudo ./release/install.sh --production-secrets` (release/install.ps1
# -ProductionSecrets on Windows) creates it, moves the line below out of an
# older secrets.env, and keeps a backup of every file it changes
# (release/secrets-upgrade/README.md).
#
# What Alembic connects as: the schema OWNER, the Postgres image's bootstrap
# superuser. Until 2026-10-02 this sat in secrets.env, which every
# application service and caddy read, so a process that should hold only
# the request and system roles could connect as a role row-level security
# does not bind and that can switch off the append-only triggers. Now the
# one-shot migration job is the only container that holds it, and
# scripts/migrate_job.py refuses to run when it is missing or still carries
# a published value. The API refuses to start if it ever reaches the API.
#
# The password must be POSTGRES_PASSWORD from postgres-init.env, byte for
# byte; a mismatch is the migration job failing to sign in on first boot.
# URL-safe characters, or percent-encode them: an unencoded `@`, `:`, `/`
# or `#` silently truncates the DSN into a different one. Host `postgres`
# is the compose service name.
NOCTORNAL_MIGRATION_DATABASE_URL=postgresql+psycopg://noctornal:replace-me-owner-password@postgres:5432/noctornal
